# OWNER REVIEW
# Vesper on the Pier: her lesson under the pier (the takedown from above; levels/pier/keys/vesper_lesson.gd), and her
# night at the top of the Ferris wheel (levels/pier/keys/wheel_vesper.gd).

~ lesson_watch
Vesper [calm]: Stop there. Stay in the dark.
Vesper: Four of them. Not one of them has looked up since he was born.
Vesper: Watch the one under me.

~ lesson_teach
Vesper [calm]: Off the beam, onto him, and the knot's tied before he's finished being surprised. One move.
Vesper: Three more under the boards. They're yours.
Nim: All three?
Vesper [warm]: Unless you'd like me to do it again. I'd rather watch you.

~ lesson_done
Vesper [warm]: Good. You landed light.
Vesper: I'll be up on the wheel, where I can see the whole pier.

~ wheel
Vesper [calm]: The whole pier, from here. Every crate that comes in under the boards. Every goon on the Midway.
Vesper: And Swyne's banner over the gate. "A clean seafront." Paid for with the same money as the crates.
- Come down and help? => help
- How long have you been up here? => long

~ help
Vesper [warm]: No. You don't need me down there. You need to know that you don't.

~ long
Vesper: Since sunset. Someone has to watch.

~ adequate
Vesper [calm]: The police are on their way. They'll find him gift-wrapped.
Vesper: And a ledger full of tea parties in Primrose Close.
Nim: Was that... all right?
Vesper [warm]: Adequate.
[narrator] From Vesper, that's warm.

~ hall_after
Vesper [warm]: Primrose Close next. Sleep first. You've earned that much.

~ wheel_top
Vesper [calm]: You took your time.
Nim: It was moving.
Vesper [warm]: So was I.
